I’ve chosen an implementation that stays entirely inside the supplied semantics and avoids an unbounded program loop: it detects whitespace by comparing `txt.split()` with `[txt]`, which is equivalent on nonempty Python strings, then sums the counts of the 13 lowercase letters at odd zero-based alphabet positions. This keeps the implementation faithful while leaving recursive string processing to the fixed `split`/`count` semantics rather than adding an execution shortcut.
